name: Real repository inventory retains limits, explicit acceptance, cache and SHA boundaries
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/empty-git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/empty-git-config
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 90 context:build partial inventory | real-partial-context
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO context
expect: CLAUDE.md
ask: Does real source inspection keep progress visible and explain the excluded symlink without claiming complete context?
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 Enter / c build inventory | empty-scopes
keys: c
require-live-snap: 90 DRAFT SCOPES | real-whole-repository
expect: Inventory limited: true
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO draft
keys: f
require-live-snap: 30 Files 1..32 | first-members
keys: End
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO last-page
require-live-snap: 30 Files | last-members
expect-not: Files 1..32
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 30 Boundary: . | returned-from-members
keys: c
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO cached
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | cached-inventory
keys: a
require-live-snap: 30 Accept exact boundaries | limited-acceptance
expect: files inspected only
expect: Omitted: .cargo. Reason: ignored directory.
ask: Can the operator understand omitted and prefix-limited material and review whole-repository membership before accepting?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: acceptance-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: acceptance-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: acceptance-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: acceptance-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: acceptance-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: acceptance-paged-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 30 Prefix only: kuzushi-logo.png | recorded-prefix-paths
keys: PPage
keys: End Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Action stopped | limits-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO refused
keys: Home Enter End Enter
require-live-snap: 60 ACCEPTED SCOPES | limits-acknowledged
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO accepted
ask: Does refusal preserve the draft, then require a separate limit acknowledgement without authorizing scans or spending?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO advance
keys: Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Field 1/1 | rename-after-new-sha
keys: C-Home C-k
type: Historical source scope
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 60 Action stopped | same-tree-new-sha-refused
expect: Git revision changed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO drifted
ask: Does a new SHA with identical files refuse mutation of the old accepted scope while preserving the entered draft and historical record?
keys: Escape
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/empty-git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/empty-git-config
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | historical-no-color-restart
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/real_repository_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME @REPO restarted
ask: Does restart clearly retain historical source and inspection limits without approving the new SHA or repeating discovery work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
